                <pb facs="1444" n="1430" sameAs="frus:frus1944v01/pg1430"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00116 E.W./9–2644: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Portugal</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Norweb</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lisbon</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-26T18:00:00+01:00">September 26,
                            1944—6 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 6:04 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2988. ReEmbs 2917, September 18, 7 p.m. On seeing Sampayo yesterday, I took
                    occasion to emphasize once more the subject of war criminals referring to the
                    public action taken by Sweden in this respect. Sampayo took the attitude that we
                    were, in his opinion, becoming unduly exercised about a matter which was largely
                    hypothetical; that Portugal had no intention of placing herself in difficulties
                    over such a question which in any event might not arise at all. He was able to
                    give me no encouragement that any statement on the matter would be issued at
                    this time.</p>
                <p>Campbell also spoke to him earlier in the day on this and I am sure that Bianchi
                    who has just arrived will also express the views as reflected from his talks in
                    the Department.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Madrid by courier.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Norweb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
